# mkdocs-literate-nav requires 4-space indent for nested bullets,
# which conflicts with markdownlint MD007 (default 2). The auto-generated
# SUMMARY.md files in the catalog tree are owned by scripts/docs/gen_catalog.py
# and must keep the 4-space form so literate-nav can parse them.
docs/*/skills/SUMMARY.md
docs/*/agents/SUMMARY.md

# Raw research reports under .audits/backstage-research/ are generated working
# artifacts (Workflow-harness synthesis), not curated docs. They use an inline
# [n] citation style with a trailing Sources list, which markdownlint reads as
# undefined reference links (MD052) and bare URLs (MD034). They are tracked so
# spec/ and skill-review references resolve, but are intentionally not prose-linted.
.audits/backstage-research/*.md
